<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Hannezo et al. (2017) Cell & Scheele et al. (2017) Nature unifying theory of branching morphogenesis via branching and annihilating random walks (BARW) (Mus musculus (mouse pubertal mammary gland, embryonic metanephric kidney, embryonic pancreas, and salivary gland ductal networks))",
        "Hannezo et al. (2017) Cell & Scheele et al. (2017) Nature unifying theory of branching morphogenesis via branching and annihilating random walks (BARW) faithfully reproduces Mus musculus (mouse pubertal mammary gland, embryonic metanephric kidney, embryonic pancreas, and salivary gland ductal networks) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Mus musculus (mouse pubertal mammary gland, embryonic metanephric kidney, embryonic pancreas, and salivary gland ductal networks) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 46.6/100, audit 2026-10-19-branching-random-walk-annihilation-audit) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py> ;
    schema:about "Mus musculus (mouse pubertal mammary gland, embryonic metanephric kidney, embryonic pancreas, and salivary gland ductal networks)" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py; output: docs/media/branching_random_walk_annihilation_comparison.png; organism: Mus musculus (mouse pubertal mammary gland, embryonic metanephric kidney, embryonic pancreas, and salivary gland ductal networks); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: 8396b081dd41f5428f101435bc6396b6e50c4b756e20f4883dc6ac81bd4c137b; artifact_sha256: a8730e1f88a086fe1b125384633e84ab0d8556565ef7d3117c23b5e9c49fb83b; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/branching_random_walk_annihilation/branching_random_walk_annihilation_reference.json=d85ad5c91bd80050..., datasets/branching_random_walk_annihilation/mouse_branched_ductal_network_specimen.jpg=d8946f47dcc4d313..., datasets/branching_random_walk_annihilation/paper_citations.bib=521cc284892baf9f..., datasets/branching_random_walk_annihilation/scout_manifest.json=8b04ea70e9991ba0...}" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2017.08.026>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature21060>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-023-39124-x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.147645> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-code-traceability>,
