<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hannezo et al. (2017) Cell & Scheele et al. (2017) Nature unifying theory of branching morphogenesis via branching and annihilating random walks (BARW) — Code-to-model traceability: 64/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Functions have brief docstrings (L34-106), but do not map code blocks to numbered equations in Hannezo et al. (2017) STAR Methods Eqs. (1)-(10), Scheele et al. (2017) Nature, Silberstein & Daniel (1987) Science, or the 3 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems in `morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_056_branching_random_walk_annihilation.lean`." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py L34–L106: Brief docstrings without equation-level or Lean 4 theorem cross-references <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py#L34-L106>" ;
    pk:hasScore 6.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hannezo et al. (2017) Cell & Scheele et al. (2017) Nature unifying theory of branching morphogenesis via branching and annihilating random walks (BARW) — Model fidelity to source: 56/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Integrates the 1D mean-field BARW reaction-diffusion PDE for active tips a(x, t) and inactive ducts i(x, t) (L51-89) and computes basic algebraic ratios (L34-48). However, `build_simple_galton_watson_tree` (L92-106) is a synthetic exponential curve rather than an off-lattice 2D spatial BARW simulator with persistent active tips, Poisson bifurcation (A -> 2A), trail deposition (A -> A + I), and tip-duct annihilation within radius R_a (A + I -> I). Multi-organ universality (mammary, kidney, pancreas) and R_a = 0 ablation controls are absent." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py L92–L106: Synthetic exponential placeholder lacking 2D off-lattice spatial BARW tip-duct annihilation <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py#L92-L106>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-model-fidelity-1> ;
    pk:hasScore 5.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hannezo et al. (2017) Cell & Scheele et al. (2017) Nature unifying theory of branching morphogenesis via branching and annihilating random walks (BARW) — Morphometric validation: 46/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L172-179) reports only 3 scalar numbers (l_branch_wt, i_homeostatic_wt, q_branch_baseline) without statistical dispersion metrics (RMSE, Pearson r, CV), without comparison to Hannezo et al. (2017) generational branching probabilities across mammary gland, kidney, and pancreas, and without perturbation deltas for TGF-beta / R_a variations or R_a = 0 non-annihilating explosion ablation." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
