<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hannezo et al. (2017) Cell & Scheele et al. (2017) Nature unifying theory of branching morphogenesis via branching and annihilating random walks (BARW) — MorphoEval overall 46.6/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 (v1 baseline) evaluation of `2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py` (51.8/100). The v1 script computes the mean-field steady-state duct density i_inf = k_b / k_a and characteristic branch length l_b = v_0 / k_b, integrates a 1D mean-field travelling-wave PDE for active tips a(x, t) and inactive ducts i(x, t), and plots an analytic S^(-3/2) curve. However, v1 lacks an off-lattice 2D spatial Branching and Annihilating Random Walk (BARW) ductal tree simulator with explicit persistent tip migration (v_0), Poisson tip bifurcation (k_b), ductal trail deposition (A -> A + I), and steric/TGF-beta tip-duct annihilation within radius R_a (A + I -> I); omits universal collapse across mouse mammary gland, kidney, and pancreas regimes; omits R_a perturbation and R_a = 0 non-annihilating explosion ablation controls; neither loads nor verifies `datasets/branching_random_walk_annihilation/branching_random_walk_annihilation_reference.json`; and performs zero computer-vision segmentation on `datasets/branching_random_walk_annihilation/mouse_branched_ductal_network_specimen.jpg`. Overall 46.6/100 (faithfulness 39.3, reproducibility 63.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 56, Morphological realism / specimen match 20, Parameter expressivity 44, Morphometric validation 46, Source and data traceability 58, Code-to-model traceability 64, Reproducibility package 68. Output judged: docs/media/branching_random_walk_annihilation_comparison.png: rendered output of 2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py at 8871db0, image/png, 111422 B, 1890×588 px, artifact_sha256 a8730e1f88a086fe1b125384633e84ab0d8556565ef7d3117c23b5e9c49fb83b (sha256 a8730e1f88a086fe1b125384633e84ab0d8556565ef7d3117c23b5e9c49fb83b), spec_fingerprint 8396b081dd41f5428f101435bc6396b6e50c4b756e20f4883dc6ac81bd4c137b. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 8396b081dd41f5428f101435bc6396b6e50c4b756e20f4883dc6ac81bd4c137b; artifact_sha256: a8730e1f88a086fe1b125384633e84ab0d8556565ef7d3117c23b5e9c49fb83b; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/branching_random_walk_annihilation/branching_random_walk_annihilation_reference.json=d85ad5c91bd80050..., datasets/branching_random_walk_annihilation/mouse_branched_ductal_network_specimen.jpg=d8946f47dcc4d313..., datasets/branching_random_walk_annihilation/paper_citations.bib=521cc284892baf9f..., datasets/branching_random_walk_annihilation/scout_manifest.json=8b04ea70e9991ba0...}." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Expand `--self-test`, CLI parameter flags (`--kb`, `--ra`, `--v0`, `--sigma-theta`, `--ka`, `--seed`), and `measure_morphoeval()` to report >= 8 quantitative metrics with reference values, dispersion (RMSE, Pearson r, CV), and negative-control ablation deltas.",
        "remediation needed: Implement a full 2D off-lattice spatial Branching and Annihilating Random Walk (BARW) ductal network simulator where active tips migrate persistently at speed v_0 with angular noise sigma_theta, deposit immutable differentiated ductal trail segments I, bifurcate stochastically at rate k_b (A -> 2A), and irreversibly annihilate (A + I -> I) upon approaching within sensing radius R_a of any non-sibling duct.",
        "remediation needed: Load and SHA-256-verify `datasets/branching_random_walk_annihilation/branching_random_walk_annihilation_reference.json` and `mouse_branched_ductal_network_specimen.jpg` at runtime, segment the cyan/green active distal buds (A, N_term = 34) and blue/magenta differentiated ductal tree (I, N_branch = 33), and verify the exact topological identity N_term = N_branch + 1 (q_branch = 33/67 = 0.4925) and peripheral active-tip pulse localization (r/R_max = 0.783).",
        "remediation needed: Simulate the 3 Hannezo et al. (2017) organ universality regimes (Mouse Pubertal Mammary Gland, Metanephric Kidney, and Embryonic Pancreas) plus TGF-beta / R_a perturbations (reduced R_a hyper-branching, elevated R_a hypoplasia, and R_a = 0 non-annihilating exponential explosion ablation), demonstrating collapse onto the critical Galton-Watson branching probability q_branch -> 1/2 and subtree distribution P(S) ~ S^(-3/2)." ;
    pk:hasScore 4.66e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
